descript         = "SFTPGo is a full-featured file transfer server supporting SFTP, WebDAV, FTP/S and HTTP/S, with local and cloud storage backends (S3-compatible, GCS, Azure). It bundles a complete WebAdmin for managing virtual users, folders, groups, event rules and file shares, plus a WebClient so users can browse, upload and share files from the browser with optional two-factor authentication. On TOS it opens in a new browser tab; all web traffic (including WebDAV and the REST API) goes through the TOS web server route /sftpgo/ with the backend listening on loopback only. SFTP is served on port 2022. There is NO default account: the first time you open the app you are guided to create your own administrator (choose your own username and password). Accounts and data live in /var/lib/sftpgo; the server runs as a dedicated unprivileged user in a hardened systemd sandbox."
release_note         = "Bundles the official SFTPGo 2.7.5 static binary (Go, zero runtime dependencies) with the SQLite data provider. Web UIs at /sftpgo/web/admin and /sftpgo/web/client, WebDAV mount point /sftpgo/webdav/, REST API /sftpgo/api/v2/, SFTP on port 2022. FIRST LOGIN: no default username/password is preset - opening the app for the first time automatically shows a setup wizard where you create the administrator account yourself. Privacy policy: /sftpgo/privacy/."
important         = "First-time setup: there is no default account. Open http://<NAS-IP>:8181/sftpgo/ and the setup wizard will guide you through creating the administrator (your own username and password - keep them safe; two-factor authentication can be enabled afterwards in the admin profile). SFTP listens on port 2022 (open it in your firewall/router as needed); FTP is disabled by default. Privacy policy: https://<NAS-IP>:8181/sftpgo/privacy/ - the app makes no outbound connections unless you configure integrations."

